KZ3 logging hooks in the runtime, plus per-minute PSO / shader-compile statistics.

Only active when the TU is built with -DKZ3_LOG_REDIRECT_STDIO (port/kz3/CMakeLists.txt does that for the runtime
library and the PPU scaffold, together with -include port/kz3/kz3_log.h); without it every hunk compiles to the old
code, so host tests and other builds are unchanged.
- ppu_crash_report: after the [CRASH] lines, kz3_log_write_crash (logs/crash-*.txt with the last 200 log lines) and
  a MiniDumpNormal minidump beside it (dbghelp loaded at run time), then kz3_crash_notify (port/kz3/main.cpp).
- the stuck-caller exit(3) becomes kz3_log_fatal("ppu", ...) first (crash file, exit code 70).
- unresolved NIDs: once per distinct NID with lr (KZ3_LOG_ONCE_KEY), was the first 40 hits.
- sys_process_exit closes the log before the host exit(); guest TTY (sys_tty_write, console_write) goes to [tty].
- thread labels ppu:<id>, spu:<id>, spurs:<k> in the log file.
- live-draw (always, LD_PSO_STAT=0 off): [pso-stat] one line per minute of run time with PSO cache misses
  (count, total, max, >4/16/50 ms), vertex/pixel D3DCompile count/total/max, shader disk-cache hits and
  CreateGraphicsPipelineState count/total/max on the walker thread.
Not here: the HardExit (0x8CF08) override, which belongs to the 1.14 build (switch-114).

